"surp":-0.1}],"div_pay":"2026-12-15","rec_trend":null,"analyst_actions":[]},"profile":{"sector":"Financial Services","industry":"Insurance - Property & Casualty","summary":"Safety Insurance Group, Inc. provides private passenger and commercial automobile, and homeowner insurance in Massachusetts, the United States. The company offers private passenger automobile policies that provide coverage for bodily injury and property damage to others, no-fault personal injury coverage for the insured/insured's car occupants, and physical damage coverage for an insured's own vehicle for collision or other perils. It also provides commercial automobile policies that offer insurance for commercial vehicles used for business purposes, including private passenger-type vehicles, trucks, tractors and trailers, and insure individual vehicles, as well as commercial fleets; and homeowners policies, which provide coverage for homes, condominiums, and apartments for losses to a dwelling and its contents from various perils, and coverage for liability to others arising from ownership or occupancy. In addition, the company offers business owners policies that cover apartments and residential condominiums, restaurants, office condominiums, processing and services businesses, special trade contractors, and wholesalers. Further, it provides personal umbrella policies, which provide personal excess liability coverage over and above the limits of individual automobile, watercraft, and homeowner's insurance policies; dwelling fire insurance for non-owner occupied residences; and commercial umbrella, which offers an excess liability product to clients. Additionally, the company offers inland marine coverage for homeowners and business owner policies; and watercraft coverage for small and medium sized pleasure crafts. It distributes its products through independent agents. The company was formerly known as Safety Holdings Inc and changed its name to Safety Insurance Group, Inc. in April 2002. Safety Insurance Group, Inc. was founded in 1979 and is headquartered in Boston, Massachusetts.","employees":568,"website":"https://www.safetyinsurance.com","country":"United States","city":"Boston","officers":[{"name":"Mr. George Michael Murphy C.P.C.U.","title":"President, CEO & Chairperson of the Board"},{"name":"Mr. John Patrick Drago","title":"Vice President of Marketing"},{"name":"Ms. Mary Frances McConnell","title":"Vice President of Underwriting"}]},"sector_medians":{"fpe":10.78,"tpe":12.58,"ps":3.482,"pfcf":11.55,"peg":1.31,"pb":1.595,"ev_ebitda":11.14,"rev_growth":0.088,"eps_growth":0.1195,"eps_growth_fwd":0.1346,"eps_growth_next":0.1035,"div_yield":0.022,"roe":0.1288,"roa":0.01563,"de":54.51,"gross_margin":0.2344,"op_margin":0.3725,"profit_margin":0.2565,"current_ratio":1.507},"valuation":[{"k":"fpe","label":"Forward P/E","v":16.7,"sector":10.78,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"tpe","label":"TTM P/E","v":21.75,"sector":12.58,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"ps","label":"Price / Sales","v":1.19,"sector":3.482,"verdict":"Undervalued"},{"k":"pfcf","label":"Price / FCF","v":10.37,"sector":11.55,"verdict":"Fairly valued"},{"k":"peg","label":"PEG","v":0.95,"sector":1.31,"verdict":"Undervalued"},{"k":"pb","label":"Price / Book","v":1.791,"sector":1.595,"verdict":"Fairly valued"},{"k":"de","label":"Debt / Equity (%)","v":6.905,"sector":54.51,"verdict":"Low debt"},{"k":"rev_growth","label":"Revenue growth","v":0.004,"sector":0.088,"verdict":"Weak"},{"k":"eps_growth","label":"EPS growth (last qtr, y/y)","v":0.073,"sector":0.1195,"verdict":"Weak"},{"k":"eps_growth_fwd","label":"EPS growth (this year, est.)","v":null,"sector":0.1346,"verdict":"—"},{"k":"eps_growth_next","label":"EPS growth (next year, est.)","v":null,"sector":0.1035,"verdict":"—"},{"k":"gross_margin","label":"Gross margin","v":0.08124,"sector":0.2344,"verdict":"Weak"},{"k":"op_margin","label":"Operating margin","v":0.119,"sector":0.3725,"verdict":"Weak"},{"k":"profit_margin","label":"Net margin","v":0.05462,"se